{
  "source_note": "Volcano numbers, names, summit coordinates, summit elevations (m) and countries are from the Smithsonian Institution Global Volcanism Program, Volcanoes of the World (Holocene list), read on 2026-10-10 from GVP's own map service (webservices.volcano.si.edu, WFS layer GVP-VOTW:Smithsonian_VOTW_Holocene_Volcanoes) because volcano.si.edu pages answered 'Smithsonian site temporarily unavailable'. GVP gives one point per volcano: Lewotobi is the Lewotobi complex point (264180), Anak Krakatau is GVP 'Krakatau' (262000), Sakurajima is GVP 'Aira' (282080) and Shinmoedake is GVP 'Kirishimayama' (282090). MAGMA Indonesia codes SMR, SIN, KAR and IBU are taken from MAGMA VONA notice numbers (e.g. 2026SMR1920); KRA, LWK and DUK follow MODULES.md and were not seen in a VONA; other Indonesian volcanoes have no code here. Aliases are the names SIGMETs, VAAs and MAGMA print. VAAC: Indonesia and Papua New Guinea DARWIN, Japan and the Philippines TOKYO. Yasur and Ambrym (Vanuatu) are left out: they are in the Wellington VAAC area, which TEPHRA's VaacCentre does not model.",
